# Testing Conventions

## Framework
- Vitest with `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` (runs in workerd runtime)
- Config: `vitest.config.ts` using `defineWorkersConfig`

## File Locations
- Unit tests: `test/unit/**/*.test.ts`
- Integration tests: `test/integration/**/*.test.ts`
- Mock data: `test/mocks/zapsign-responses.ts`

## Test Naming
- Use `describe('module/function name', () => { ... })`
- Use `it('should + expected behavior', () => { ... })`
- Group by happy path, error cases, edge cases

## Mock Conventions
- Mock `global.fetch` for API client tests
- Mock `ZapSignClient` methods for tool tests
- Use realistic data from `test/mocks/zapsign-responses.ts`
- Never mock the module under test

## Assertions
- Prefer `expect(x).toBe(y)` for primitives
- Prefer `expect(x).toEqual(y)` for objects
- Prefer `expect(fn).toThrow(ErrorClass)` for error testing
- Always assert on error properties (code, statusCode, retryable)

## Pre-commit
Run before every commit: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test`
